{"type":"message","id":"f03b46ff","parentId":"8a937055","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:47:21.940Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Worth noting that a \"Z\" input returns a timezone-aware datetime now, which is a behavior worth flagging. The unused timezone import in the test file isn't something I need to worry about.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")`. The old format string had nothing to match the trailing `Z`, which is why you got the error. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass, including `test_naive` and `test_day_key`.\n\nTwo behaviour changes to know about:\n- **Timezone-aware results:** when the input ends in `Z` or has an offset such as `+02:00`, the result now carries a timezone (`Z` becomes UTC). Inputs with no zone still come back without one, as before. If any caller compares or subtracts results from both kinds of input, Python will raise a `TypeError`.\n- **Python version:** `fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 and later. This environment runs 3.13, but the repo doesn't declare a minimum Python version, so on 3.10 or older the same `Z` input would fail again."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":387,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":26788,"totalTokens":27177,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":26788}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277237759,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8d69r239DxSM1qtWTnv","duration":4180.970649999999,"ttft":949.0845550000013,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26790,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
